etained R&D ids, mutating markdown source-of-truth) â†’ blast-radius failure.\n- It invents structure/modules not present, or misses load-bearing ones.\n\n## Stakes VECTOR\n- **Impact:** medium â€” orientation doc; wrong content wastes a new owner's time and could mislead.\n- **Reversibility:** the *report* is fully reversible (it's a doc). But the **subject system runs as a live Windows service writing to markdown source-of-truth with no DB/undo**; advice that triggers a destructive op is hard to reverse. â†’ irreversibility of the *subject* forces tier **>= medium**.\n- **Blast radius:** the report is read-only output under the research dir; constraint is \"do not mutate the working tree.\" Blast radius of the *deliverable* itself is contained.\n- **Projected tier: MEDIUM.** Phase-3 includes independent reviewer + separate judge passes.\n\n## Candidate branches\n- **B1 (chosen):** Verify-against-tree brownfield inventory â†’ fan-out sub-agents over (architecture, tests/build/run, docs+prior-work, working-tree state) â†’ cross-check doc claims vs disk â†’ synthesize orientation report + risk register. Adversarial review by independent agents.\n- **B2 (dropped):** Trust CLAUDE.md + memory as ground truth and just reformat them into a report. *Counterfactual cost of dropping:* none lost â€” this is exactly the falsification mode; CLAUDE.md is detailed but is a claim, not an observation, and the git working tree shows uncommitted drift (modified dashboards, untracked .anchor/, rnd_jobs/) that a doc-only pass would miss.\n- **B3 (dropped/deferred):** Deep per-module code audit (read every .py end-to-end). *Counterfactual cost:* lower risk of a subtle behavioral miss, but far over-scoped for an *orientation* report and would blow the budget; deferred to the \"outstanding work\" the new owner can do. Recorded as a known coverage limit.\n\n## Best-in-class baseline to beat\nA competent engineer handed the repo who runs `git log`, reads CLAUDE.md, and skims the top of each